Aether: final telemetry sweep

Optional Features section, dead pings, gecko-trace out, last Glean writers, final sweep, and the offline stub foundation.

Squashed from 6 units:

  [core/29-optional-features.patch]
  Aether: "Optional Features" section to turn on Report Broken Site
  
  Settings > Optional Features (English, off by default) with a single
  toggle. aether.optional.report-broken-site=false in firefox.js.
  With the option off: cmd_reportBrokenSite, the Help menu item and the
  protections panel button are hidden, and the reporter's submit/start
  handlers do nothing. With the option on, DEFAULT_NEW_REPORT_ENDPOINT
  (https://webcompat.com/issues/new) is restored along with the normal
  webcompat.com flow. You still have to press Send in the dialog itself.
  
  [core/30-dead-pings.patch]
  Aether: killed Glean pings (group 30)
  
  Deleted for having zero real submitters:
  - toolkit/components/glean/pings.yaml: dau-reporting (0 refs in the tree)
  - toolkit/components/reportbrokensite/pings.yaml: broken-site-report
    (submitter already neutralised) + its pytest test, which only
    compared that ping and pointed at mobile/ (deleted in group 19)
  - toolkit/components/nimbus/pings.yaml: nimbus-targeting-context
    (submitter already neutralised) and heartbeat (Normandy OFF)
  - toolkit/components/telemetry/pings.yaml: usage-reporting,
    usage-deletion-request and onboarding-opt-out. third-party-modules
    stays: its submitter (UntrustedModulesPing) is still in place.
  
  Killed plumbing that accompanied them:
  - RemoteSettingsExperimentLoader: out goes the targeting context
    registration, the nimbus.telemetry.targetingContextEnabled pref and
    the now-empty finally block.
  - SpecialMessageActions: out goes the submitOnboardingOptOutPing
    action, its case, the blocklist entry, the JSON schema and the doc,
    and the onboarding step that fired it.
  - UsageReporting/ClientID/TelemetryControllerParent: comments and
    docs describing pings that no longer exist.
  - metrics_index.py: out go glean/pings.yaml and
    reportbrokensite/pings.yaml.
  - telemetry/metrics.yaml: out goes nimbus-targeting-context from
    send_in_pings.
  
  [core/31-no-gecko-trace.patch]
  Aether: remove the gecko-trace component (group 31)
  
  Distributed tracing with OpenTelemetry. Instrumentation dead for
  three independent reasons:
  - GECKO_TRACE_ENABLE is only set with moz_debug|nightly|dev_edition,
    so in a release build GeckoTrace.cpp was not even compiled and
    GeckoTrace.h fell into its no-op branch.
  - Only GeckoTrace.cpp called recv_gecko_trace_export, and the Rust
    crate did get compiled (gkrust-shared depends on it) but nobody
    invokes it.
  - report_in_glean was a no-op (patch 12), so traces_data never had a
    writer and the gecko-trace ping was never sent.
  
  Removed: toolkit/components/gecko-trace/ and
  third_party/opentelemetry-cpp/, with the ping, its generated metrics,
  its own lint and its taskcluster jobs.
  
  Plumbing cleanup:
  - dom/{quota,cache,indexedDB,localstorage}: out go the #includes and
    the 25 GECKO_TRACE_SCOPE. In QuotaCommon.cpp also the
    DomQuotaTryEvent and its QM_LOG_ERROR_TO_TELEMETRY_ENABLED block
    (with the Config.h define).
  - xpcom: out goes SetOpenTelemetryInternalLogLevel (Logging.cpp) and
    the two Init calls (XPCOMInit.cpp).
  - IPC: out goes the GeckoTraceExport message from PContent,
    PUtilityProcess and PSocketProcess, with their RecvGeckoTraceExport.
  - Registries: toolkit/components/moz.build, shared/Cargo.toml,
    shared/lib.rs, metrics_index.py, toolkit/moz.configure, Cargo.lock,
    StaticPrefList.yaml, command_util.py (mach gecko-trace),
    vendor-verify and the protobuf generator.
  
  tools/profiler/public/GeckoTraceEvent.h is not touched: it belongs to
  the profiler.
  
  [core/32-stub-offline.patch]
  Aether: offline stub installer with no Mozilla phone-home (group 32)
  
  The stub installer (stub.nsi) is the direct-install UI: one download/install
  page, no wizard. Two changes make it ours:
  
  - Offline payload. scripts/make-stub-offline.py packs setup-stub.exe together
    with the full installer (as aether-full.exe) inside the SFX exe. When the
    stub finds aether-full.exe next to itself, StartDownload copies it to
    $PLUGINSDIR\\download.exe and jumps straight to LaunchFullInstaller: no
    download from Mozilla, no Mozilla cert check on our own payload (an unsigned
    dev build could never pass it). Without the bundled file the stub falls back
    to downloading, so a bare setup-stub.exe still behaves like upstream.
  - No telemetry. Install and uninstall pings POSTed to Mozilla on every run,
    with no gating, plus a post-uninstall survey opened in Edge and an
    installation_telemetry.json feeding the (removed) in-app telemetry.
    All sends are gone: stub and full install-ping paths, the uninstall POST,
    the survey page and its opener, the telemetry JSON, and the launcher
    telemetry opt-out is now opt-out. HttpPostFile.dll leaves the plugin set;
    nsJSON stays (the version check still parses JSON). Ping builders and
    TELEMETRY_* defines stay for the NSIS tests, which do not build here.
    Zero Mozilla network on a fresh install (the version check only runs with
    a previous same-channel install present).
  
  Per-user default needs no patch: getDefaultInstallDir already picks
  %LOCALAPPDATA%\\Aether Browser when the account cannot write Program Files,
  so a non-admin install never elevates.
  
  Deliberately NOT touched: the uninstaller itself (helper.exe still ships
  inside the browser and the updater runs it), the maintenance service, NSIS
  as a toolchain, and `mach repackage`/upload-files.mk/MSI-MSIX (never run
  with MOZ_PKG_FORMAT=ZIP).
  
  [core/33-last-glean-writers.patch]
  Aether: the last Glean writers in the product.
  
  After the previous telemetry patches, six recording calls were still live in
  shipped code (everything else was either in tests or in the glean machinery
  itself):
  
    dom/quota/ActorsParent.cpp
      - glean::dom_quota::shutdown_time    (QuotaManager::ShutdownInstance)
      - glean::dom_quota::info_load_time  (QuotaManager::LoadQuota)
    toolkit/components/crashes/CrashManager.in.sys.mjs
      - Glean.crash.compressedStoreSize   (CrashStore._writeData)
      - Glean.crash.submitAttempt         (CrashStore.addSubmission)
      - Glean.crash.submitSuccess         (CrashStore.addSubmissionResult)
    toolkit/components/glean/ipc/Support.cpp
      - fog_ipc::shutdown_registration_failures (FOG_RegisterShutdownFlush)
  
  Removed:
    - RecordTimeDeltaHelper and its Start/End/Run. It existed only to feed the two
      quota metrics, including the OS suspend/wake handling the metric needed.
    - The DomQuotaMetrics.h include.
  
  Kept on purpose, do not "clean these up":
    - startTime/endTime in LoadQuota. They feed the slow-load check guarded by
      dom_quotaManager_checkQuotaInfoLoadTime, which is not telemetry. They are
      now plain TimeStamp::Now() readings.
    - The crash submission bookkeeping (requestDate, responseDate, result): local
      state, not measurement.
    - The NS_WARNING in FOG_RegisterShutdownFlush: a local diagnostic about a
      real leaked runnable.
    - gLastOSWake: still written, no longer read (Run() was its only reader).
  
  Second pass: the writers the first sweep could not see, because their
  receiver carries no glean:: prefix or is a whole subsystem.
  
    toolkit/components/glean/ipc/FOGIPC.cpp
      - fog_ipc::flush_durations (Start/Cancel/StopAndAccumulate),
        flush_rejections, flush_failures and buffer_sizes: the metrics the
        FOG IPC flush pipeline records about itself. The pipeline stays;
        only its self-measurement goes.
      - power_cpu_ms_per_thread and power_wakeups_per_thread: twelve
        per-thread recordings in RecordThreadCpuUse(). That function was
        already dead code, its only caller (the profiler's thread
        registration) having been removed by an earlier patch, so the
        function, the ProcessType enum and the gThisProcessType global it
        shared with RecordPowerMetrics are gone too. RecordPowerMetrics
        itself stays: it only feeds profiler markers now, and the profiler
        is a developer tool, not telemetry.
    xpcom/base/MemoryTelemetry.cpp and .h, deleted whole
      The Glean memory-telemetry subsystem: ten recordings (heap_allocated,
      heap_overhead_fraction, collection_time, total,
      distribution_among_content, and the RECORD_* macro family with their
      twenty call sites). Nothing else in the file does non-telemetry work,
      so the subsystem goes whole, with all of its wiring:
        xpcom/base/moz.build (the source and the exported header)
        toolkit/components/telemetry/core/Telemetry.cpp (the member, the
          EarlyInit/DelayedInit/Shutdown lifecycle, GatherMemory)
        toolkit/components/telemetry/core/nsITelemetry.idl (gatherMemory)
        TelemetrySession.sys.mjs (its three gatherMemory() calls)
        js/xpconnect/src/XPCJSContext.cpp (the Poke-after-each-task block)
        dom/ipc/ContentChild.cpp (an include that was already unused)
    xpcom/base/PHCManager.cpp and .h
      - ReportPHCTelemetry and its declaration; slop, slots_allocated and
        slots_freed were its only reason to exist. PHC itself (the
        probabilities, the size, the pref callbacks) is untouched.
    widget/windows/nsLookAndFeel.cpp
      - touch_enabled_device. The constructor stays, as a
        plain "= default": the class holds a UniquePtr to the
        forward-declared KeyWatcher, so it needs a user-provided
        constructor defined in the .cpp, where WinRegistry.h
        makes KeyWatcher complete (an implicit one would be
        instantiated by the "new nsLookAndFeel()" in
        nsXPLookAndFeel.cpp, in translation units that only
        see the forward declaration).
    xpcom/base/nsMemoryReporterManager.cpp
      - free_purged_pages, the timer around the jemalloc purge.
    widget/cocoa/nsMenuBarX.mm
      - mac_application_menu_opened (macOS only; does not compile here).
    widget/cocoa/nsDeviceContextSpecX.mm
      - printing.target_type, three print-session paths (macOS only).
  
  After this, no shipped file calls a Glean recording method. The JS side was
  already clean: no shipped JS imports services-glean, and the wrapper modules
  the first pass flagged (ExtensionTelemetry, AutofillTelemetry, MLTelemetry,
  BrowserSearchTelemetry, SearchSERPTelemetry, UrlbarTelemetryUtils,
  SmartWindowTelemetry, TargetingContextRecorder, UserCharacteristicsPageService)
  are no-op shells whose recording bodies earlier patches emptied; they log to
  the console or do nothing.
  
  The metric definitions stay in the metrics.yaml files they live in, plus
  third-party-modules in toolkit/components/telemetry/pings.yaml; they now have
  no writers. Deleting the definitions is separate work because metrics_index.py
  lists them and 21 patches edit that file.
  
  Note for auditors: grepping for `Glean.` does NOT prove that nothing records.
  Wrapper modules hold the metric object as a parameter and call methods on it.
  The reliable test is the import: nothing outside tests imports
  services-glean, so no JS in the product can reach a Glean metric at all.
  
  [core/34-final-cleanup-sweep.patch]
  Aether: final cleanup sweep
  
  The last of the removal work, folded together because none of it is worth a
  patch of its own any more:
  
  * the final Glean sweep: the last live recording sites in shipped code, the
    self-measurements inside the vendored SDK, and every remaining production
    metric and ping definition;
  * the installer telemetry: the dead code, the phase-timing vars and the ping
    that went out after an uninstall;
  * the MSI and MSIX sources, which this build never generated (MOZ_PKG_FORMAT
    is ZIP) and which contradicted the per-user, no-UAC installer;
  * an orphaned `try` in the Nimbus experiment loader whose `finally` an earlier
    patch removed, leaving a module that never parsed.
  
  With this, `MOZILLA_OFFICIAL` is off, the Glean uploader is inert and no ping
  definition survives in production code.
